        "original_id": "b9b9bc72-5a8d-5a8b-b586-a0a1d2341337",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: LD Beghtol, Damian Costilla\n- Bands: Flare Acoustic Arts League, The Magnetic Fields, The Smiths, Love, The Velvet Underground\n- Albums: 69 Love Songs\n- Companies: Merge Records\n- Places: Fort Campbell, Kentucky, New York\n- Topics: American musicians, art directors, writers, experimental pop, indie pop, musical influences\n\nFacts:\n- LD Beghtol was born in 1964 in Fort Campbell, Kentucky.\n- LD Beghtol is an American musician, art director, and writer.\n- Flare Acoustic Arts League, also known as Flare, was formed in New York in 1996 by guitarist Damian Costilla and singer LD Beghtol.\n- Flare Acoustic Arts League was an experimental pop band known for intense, darkly romantic, atmospheric songs.\n- Flare Acoustic Arts League was influenced by The Smiths, The Magnetic Fields, Love, various 4AD bands, and The Velvet Underground.\n- LD Beghtol sometimes collaborated with The Magnetic Fields.\n- 69 Love Songs is the sixth studio album by the American indie pop band The Magnetic Fields.\n- 69 Love Songs was released on September 7, 1999 by Merge Records.",
